[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/pulls/1229","id":5426628168,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUABPTs8AAAABQ3PGSA","html_url":"https://github.com/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/pull/1229","diff_url":"https://github.com/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/pull/1229.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/pull/1229.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/issues/1229","number":1229,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"protocol: a box test's refusal is read only in a box that stood, and only as the refusal its tamper expects, so the hands:: tests no longer fail beside probe:: (#1187)","user":{"login":"valentinyanakiev","id":7090348,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTAzNDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7090348?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/valentinyanakiev","html_url":"https://github.com/valentinyanakiev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valentinyanakiev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valentinyanakiev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valentinyanakiev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valentinyanakiev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valentinyanakiev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valentinyanakiev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valentinyanakiev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valentinyanakiev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valentinyanakiev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #1187. The `hands::` box tests no longer fail beside `probe::` at 16 threads. A box test now reads a refusal only once its box is shown to have stood, and only as the exact refusal its tamper expects.\n\nBrokkr-Run: landing-over-an-existing-branch--5b5ccd50\nRuling: #1187 (https://github.com/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/issues/1187#issuecomment-7060897111), standing ruling 2026-11-04 \"go with recommended\" and \"and by hand\": the last run parked REVIEW-REFORGE-EXHAUSTED-MEDIUM on two test-code MEDIUMs. The controller fixed both by hand, restacked and re-signed the branch, and it lands with the `by-hand` label.\n\n- **The cause:** `hands::` also matches `adapters::dsh_hands::`. There, `a_linked_worktree_runner_is_not_a_hands_launch` put `bwrap -> /bin/true` first on the process `PATH`. Every box test beside it resolved bubblewrap through that `PATH`, so a box either \"ran\" as `/bin/true` (exit 0) or found no `bwrap` at all once the guard dropped. Every failure in #1187 was one of the two.\n- **The fix:** that test now runs in its own engine, so its stand-in leads only its child's `PATH`.\n- **The proof a box stood:** a box test reads a refusal only after the box hands back its own HOME. A box that never stood fails as \"not established\".\n- **The exact refusal:** each tamper names the exit code and the reason its stderr must end with. The reasons are measured per system: uutils, GNU coreutils and BusyBox. A tamper that never ran (127), one killed by a signal (137) or one cut off at its deadline fails the test. So does one refused for another reason, including an operand whose own text ends in the refusal's words.\n- **The tamper's target:** each tamper names its path as one bash `$'…'` word, byte for byte. A `$`, a space, a quote, a backslash or a byte that is not UTF-8 in the temporary directory never moves it to another path.\n- **Test code only.** No production line changes, and the public API is unchanged.\n\n**History:** three runs, nine commits.\n1. `fix-issue-1187-the-hands-box-tes-798fdd52`: the cause, the fix and the stood-box proof. It parked REVIEW-REFORGE-EXHAUSTED-MEDIUM: any non-zero exit after the marker passed as a refusal.\n2. `finish-issue-1187-a-box-test-s-r-92294654`: exact refusals, the 127 and 137 controls, and quoted tamper paths. This was the Qwen-chief trial's run, with reviews 4 and 5. It parked at its final review on the provider's exhausted quota.\n3. `landing-over-an-existing-branch--5b5ccd50`, under the house Astra chief: the refusal is the reason the whole stderr ends with. It parked REVIEW-REFORGE-EXHAUSTED-MEDIUM on two MEDIUMs.\n\n**Controller commit on the restack** onto main 32db5f238 (d66801d2d), closing the landing review's two MEDIUMs:\n- **`shell_quoted` kept a lossy path.** It quoted `Path::display()`, which replaces bytes that are not UTF-8, so an outside-root tamper could meet ENOENT on another path and pass the absent-root check. It now writes the path byte for byte. A new control, `a_quoted_path_that_is_not_utf8_names_its_own_bytes`, plants the lossy name beside the real one and fails under the old quoting.\n- **The quoting control read login profiles.** It ran host bash with `-lc`, so a profile could change `PATH` or define `cat`. It now runs `bash -c` with the cleared environment. The box itself still runs `bash -lc` under its own private HOME.\n- **A move:** `shell_quoted` and its controls moved to `hands/tests/quoted.rs`. evidence.rs had reached the 2000-line test ceiling; it is now 1974 lines.\n\n**Checked by the controller** on the ripper, at d66801d2d on main 32db5f238:\n- fmt, and clippy `--workspace --all-targets --all-features -D warnings`;\n- brokkr-protocol `--lib` `hands:: probe::` at 16 threads, three runs. Two passed all 446 tests. One failed only `hands::session::tests::the_listing_removes_nothing_and_counts_what_the_reaping_would`, the known flake #1157, in code this branch doesn't touch.\n- The evidence pair passes with `BROKKR_REQUIRE_BOUNDARY_EVIDENCE=1`, in a real namespace. Both `quoted::` controls pass.\n- brokkr-runtime `--lib` `hands`: 70 passed;\n- typos, the files, clones and api ratchets, and `git diff --check`.\n\nCI's exact coverage gate, CRAP ratchet and macOS legs are CI's.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-11-21T09:56:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-21T11:52:24Z","closed_at":"2026-11-21T11:51:20Z","merged_at":"2026-11-21T11:51:20Z","merge_commit_sha":"41e000e4e600c796035abdb01d98e324954922f6","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":12041376294,"node_id":"LA_kwDOUABPTs8AAAACzbjSJg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/labels/by-hand","name":"by-hand","color":"B60205","default":false,"description":"Operator-only escape hatch for 'delivered by brokkr' (decision 0033)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/pulls/1229/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/pulls/1229/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/issues/1229/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/statuses/d66801d2d178fcb33ccb72ad03ece718eb3d8f61","head":{"label":"feedback-loop-ai:story-1187-land","ref":"story-1187-land","sha":"d66801d2d178fcb33ccb72ad03ece718eb3d8f61","user":{"login":"feedback-loop-ai","id":250017135,"node_id":"O_kgDODub1bw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250017135?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/feedback-loop-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/feedback-loop-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feedback-loop-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feedback-loop-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feedback-loop-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feedback-loop-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feedback-loop-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feedback-loop-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/user